WHAT THIS VERIFIES AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
---------------------------------------
VERIFIED in ~1 s: the engine's move generator matches the PUBLISHED perft chain on the start position to depth 5
(20 / 400 / 8,902 / 197,281 / 4,865,609), and python-chess's independent walker agrees to depth 4. So the walker used
throughout this seat's comparisons is anchored on a known answer, which is the claim PERFT_NULL_RESULT.md makes about
itself in its first line.

NOT RE-RUN: the 5,000-position sweeps and the depth-5 totals (7,399,207,740 / 1,022,355,864 / 2,603,588,130). Those are
hours of compute and their raw outputs are on disk; the one I spot-checked — the seed-2301 perft-4 total of 154,284 for
position 1 in `job1/compare_R.out` — matches. Re-running them would test the machine's stability over the session, not
the claim, and the claim already carries its own control (a planted one-node mismatch was caught, per 23-F3).

THE HONEST STATEMENT FOR THE FINAL: the perft null result's ANCHOR is re-verified today; its BULK rests on saved outputs
whose checker was itself proved able to fail.
